Author: Paul Clark <systemslibrarian@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 18 21:16:37 2026 -0400

    fix(C16,C23): ea_restart computes the 3.1.4.3 cutoff exactly and refuses an H_I whose scale it cannot establish
    
    C23 (upstream code, OC-27): simulateBound() took the (1-alpha) order
    statistic of the simulated MAXIMUM over all 2^H_I symbols where 3.1.4.3
    step 5 specifies one Binomial(1000, p) tail; its cutoff sat 2-5 counts
    above the standard's at every H_I and accepted matrices the standard
    rejects. X_cutoff is now exactBound(0.000005, H_I): the largest x with
    Pr[X >= x] >= alpha, summed in long double; equal to an exact-rational
    evaluation at 32 values of H_I (0.25..8). -s accepted and ignored.
    
    C16 (OC-11/OC-28): the H_I argument has an explicit grammar; underflow
    (1e-400 -> 0) and H_I <= 0 are refused; for a multi-bit symbol the scale
    must be stated, '<v>/symbol' or '<v>/bit', because a per-bit figure given
    bare passes every range check and yields a wrong cutoff silently (0.875
    bare on 8-bit: cutoff 615 against 23). Bare numbers remain valid for 1-bit
    symbols.
    
    The report carries restartHI, restartAlpha, restartXmax, restartXcutoff and
    passedRestartSanityCheck so a consumer can recompute the decision.
    
    Four-state matrix (reproducers/c16-c23-matrix.sh, audit knobs
    EA_RESTART_WITHOUT_C16_FIX / _C23_FIX): neither fix accepts all three bad
    inputs; C16 alone still accepts X_max 24 at cutoff 27; C23 alone still
    accepts 1e-400 (cutoff 1000) and the bare wrong-scale H_I (cutoff 614);
    both close the gate.
    
    regression-restart.sh: C16+C23 section, PASS on the repaired build, FAIL
    against the tag build (logs/c23/regression-restart-vs-tag.log). Callers
    updated to the /symbol form; the N-10 case moved from H_I 0 to a
    checkerboard at H_I 1. Full suite: 20 passed, 0 failed.
    
    No published figure rests on a restart acceptance (no real restart dataset
    exists), so nothing moves; XR-10 tells TruePad the January run must be
    decided by the exact test. Self-authored and unreviewed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

